WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.986
<v Examiner>Exam case 8, continued.

2
00:00:02.986 --> 00:00:06.893
<v Examiner>Rheumatoid arthritis, cortisol, and what to tell Shannon.

3
00:00:07.343 --> 00:00:08.027
<v Examiner>Four marks.

4
00:00:08.027 --> 00:00:10.265
<v Examiner>What occurs in rheumatoid arthritis?

5
00:00:10.715 --> 00:00:13.894
The hook: autoimmune, fast, both sides, whole body.

6
00:00:14.344 --> 00:00:17.480
It's autoimmune: the immune system attacks the joints.

7
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.707
The onset is relatively rapid, over weeks to months, and it can begin at any time in life.

8
00:00:22.707 --> 00:00:25.146
The joints are painful, swollen and stiff,

9
00:00:25.146 --> 00:00:29.792
often small and large joints on both sides of the body: both hands, both wrists,

10
00:00:29.792 --> 00:00:31.766
the elbows, the balls of the feet.

11
00:00:31.766 --> 00:00:34.321
Morning stiffness lasts longer than an hour.

12
00:00:34.321 --> 00:00:39.432
And there are whole-body symptoms: frequent fatigue, and a general feeling of being ill.

13
00:00:39.882 --> 00:00:40.388
<v Examiner>One mark.

14
00:00:40.388 --> 00:00:42.805
<v Examiner>What is the other type of arthritis called?

15
00:00:43.255 --> 00:00:44.258
Osteoarthritis.

16
00:00:44.258 --> 00:00:45.729
The wear and tear one.

17
00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:47.852
<v Examiner>Four marks.

18
00:00:47.852 --> 00:00:52.193
<v Examiner>What is the difference between osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis?

19
00:00:52.643 --> 00:00:57.208
Her table has four rows: the cause, the onset, the joints, and the whole body.

20
00:00:57.658 --> 00:00:58.339
The cause.

21
00:00:58.339 --> 00:01:00.043
Rheumatoid is autoimmune.

22
00:01:00.043 --> 00:01:02.223
Osteoarthritis is wear and tear.

23
00:01:02.673 --> 00:01:03.356
The onset.

24
00:01:03.356 --> 00:01:08.544
Rheumatoid can begin at any time in life, and comes on over weeks to months.

25
00:01:08.544 --> 00:01:12.913
Osteoarthritis usually begins later in life, slowly, over years.

26
00:01:13.363 --> 00:01:14.036
The joints.

27
00:01:14.036 --> 00:01:19.052
In rheumatoid, they're painful, swollen and stiff, on both sides, small and large,

28
00:01:19.052 --> 00:01:21.744
with morning stiffness of more than an hour.

29
00:01:21.744 --> 00:01:26.332
In osteoarthritis there's aching and tenderness with little or no swelling,

30
00:01:26.332 --> 00:01:31.042
usually in one set of joints, like the fingers, thumbs, hips, knees or spine,

31
00:01:31.042 --> 00:01:33.673
and morning stiffness of less than an hour.

32
00:01:34.123 --> 00:01:35.109
The whole body.

33
00:01:35.109 --> 00:01:39.118
Rheumatoid has whole-body symptoms: fatigue, and feeling ill.

34
00:01:39.118 --> 00:01:40.629
Osteoarthritis doesn't.

35
00:01:42.079 --> 00:01:42.665
<v Examiner>Two marks.

36
00:01:42.665 --> 00:01:46.005
<v Examiner>Where is cortisol produced and secreted from in the body?

37
00:01:46.455 --> 00:01:51.734
In the adrenal glands: paired, pyramid-shaped glands on top of the kidneys.

38
00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:55.183
Specifically, the adrenal cortex, the outer part.

39
00:01:55.183 --> 00:02:00.462
Cortisol is its main glucocorticoid, and its release is stimulated by ACTH,

40
00:02:00.462 --> 00:02:02.433
from the anterior pituitary.

41
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:03.527
<v Examiner>Four marks.

42
00:02:03.527 --> 00:02:08.387
<v Examiner>What are the functions of cortisol, and how is this related to the stress response?

43
00:02:08.837 --> 00:02:12.549
The hook: more sugar, steady blood volume, and less inflammation.

44
00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:18.044
Cortisol increases blood glucose, by forming glucose from non-carbohydrate sources,

45
00:02:18.044 --> 00:02:19.563
which is gluconeogenesis.

46
00:02:19.563 --> 00:02:22.906
It also raises the blood's fatty acids and amino acids.

47
00:02:22.906 --> 00:02:26.370
It prepares the body to resist chronic, long-term stress,

48
00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:30.807
by keeping blood sugar relatively constant, and maintaining blood volume.

49
00:02:30.807 --> 00:02:33.967
Maintaining blood volume keeps the tissues perfused,

50
00:02:33.967 --> 00:02:37.492
so oxygen and nutrients are there to deal with the stress.

51
00:02:37.492 --> 00:02:41.382
And it reduces inflammation, so less swelling, redness and pain,

52
00:02:41.382 --> 00:02:43.570
and it suppresses the immune system.

53
00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:45.642
<v Examiner>Two marks.

54
00:02:45.642 --> 00:02:49.436
<v Examiner>How is cortisol going to help Shannon's rheumatoid arthritis?

55
00:02:49.886 --> 00:02:50.492
Two ways.

56
00:02:50.492 --> 00:02:55.269
It reduces inflammation: less swelling, redness and pain in her joints.

57
00:02:55.269 --> 00:02:58.701
And it suppresses the immune system, which matters,

58
00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:01.594
because rheumatoid arthritis is autoimmune:

59
00:03:01.594 --> 00:03:04.891
an overactive immune system attacking her joints.

60
00:03:04.891 --> 00:03:08.659
Prednisone is the synthetic version, doing the same job.

61
00:03:09.109 --> 00:03:09.637
<v Examiner>Two marks.

62
00:03:09.637 --> 00:03:12.224
<v Examiner>What might you say to Shannon about her concerns?

63
00:03:12.674 --> 00:03:17.832
Her own words from the session: rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune condition,

64
00:03:17.832 --> 00:03:19.509
and it can hit at any age.

65
00:03:19.509 --> 00:03:21.766
So Shannon is not too young for it.

66
00:03:21.766 --> 00:03:26.989
It's not the wear and tear of osteoarthritis, which usually begins later in life.

67
00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:28.083
<v Examiner>Once more.

68
00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:30.340
<v Examiner>Rheumatoid arthritis, and cortisol.

69
00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.970
Rheumatoid arthritis is autoimmune.

70
00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.774
It comes on over weeks to months, at any age,

71
00:03:37.774 --> 00:03:41.823
affects joints on both sides with morning stiffness over an hour,

72
00:03:41.823 --> 00:03:43.692
and brings whole-body fatigue.

73
00:03:43.692 --> 00:03:48.551
Osteoarthritis is wear and tear: later in life, over years, one set of joints,

74
00:03:48.551 --> 00:03:52.849
little swelling, stiffness under an hour, and no whole-body symptoms.

75
00:03:52.849 --> 00:03:56.400
Cortisol comes from the adrenal cortex, released by ACTH.

76
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.079
It raises blood glucose by gluconeogenesis,

77
00:03:59.079 --> 00:04:04.250
keeps blood volume and perfusion up through long-term stress, reduces inflammation,

78
00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:08.236
and suppresses the immune system, which is how it helps Shannon.

79
00:04:08.236 --> 00:04:11.787
And tell her: it's autoimmune, and it can hit at any age.
